## The Total Ring Number

Planning a ring as "stone price" and "setting price" as separate budgets is the most common mistake buyers make. The Total Ring Number treats them as one number from the start.

[![Radiant cut diamond ring white gold pavé band setting on display](/images/radiant-cut-ring-white-gold-pave-band.avif)](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings?ShapeID=Radiant&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)

For a radiant cut, the right split is 75–80% on the stone, 20–25% on the setting. The radiant cut is a brilliance-forward shape. The 70 facets do the visual work. A beautiful $1,500 setting on a mediocre VS2-with-visible-inclusions radiant is a waste of $1,500. Put the budget on the stone. Then pick a clean, well-made setting that gets out of the way.

**Setting prices and your stone budget at common totals:**

