**Reading this data.** The entry natural ring is a [1ct G-VS2 at $3,818 total](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/25995245?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). G colour is white-facing and eye-clean. VS2 clarity is completely invisible to the naked eye. This is a legitimate natural GIA ring for under $4,000. The 2ct natural jumps to $19,214 minimum — that is the carat premium in this market. If 2ct natural is above budget, go lab. You get the same visual size for $3,669.

> "Natural radiant cuts are one of the best-value natural diamonds in the market right now. They are undervalued compared to rounds and ovals at the same carat weight. A 1ct G-VS2 GIA radiant at $2,318 for the stone is a deal by any comparison. The same colour and clarity in a round brilliant costs significantly more.
>
> One thing I always confirm on natural radiants is the L/W ratio. I've had buyers order a 'radiant cut' expecting an elongated stone and receive something much closer to a square. Always verify the ratio from the certificate. It's not optional." — Farzana Hasan, **[Diamond Critics](https://diamondcritics.com/about-farzana/)**

