## Natural vs Lab Radiant: Direct Comparison

<table class="dc-custom-table"><thead><tr><th>Comparison</th><th>Natural Radiant</th><th>Lab Radiant</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1ct G-VS2 stone price</td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/25995245?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational"><strong>$2,318</strong></a></td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29417414?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational"><strong>$867 (E-VVS1)</strong></a></td></tr><tr><td>Total ring at 1ct + Solitaire WG</td><td><strong>$3,463</strong></td><td><strong>$2,012</strong></td></tr><tr><td>2ct stone price</td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/16750163?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational"><strong>$17,714 (D-VS2)</strong></a></td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/27801066?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational"><strong>$2,169 (F-VVS1)</strong></a></td></tr><tr><td>Total ring at 2ct + Riviera Pavé WG</td><td><strong>$19,214</strong></td><td><strong>$3,669</strong></td></tr><tr><td>Resale value</td><td>20–40% of purchase</td><td>Near zero</td></tr><tr><td>Certificate</td><td>GIA preferred</td><td>IGI or GIA</td></tr><tr><td>Visual difference</td><td>None visible</td><td>None visible</td></tr><tr><td>Clarity floor for radiant</td><td>VS2</td><td>VS2</td></tr><tr><td>Colour recommendation</td><td>G–H for WG, H–I for YG/RG</td><td>E–F for any metal</td></tr></tbody></table>

The visual difference between a natural and lab radiant is zero. A gemologist cannot tell them apart without specialist equipment. If resale value matters to you in a meaningful way, choose natural. If it doesn't — and for most buyers it shouldn't, since you're not buying a ring to sell it — lab is the rational choice at this price difference.

