## FAQ

### What is a radiant cut engagement ring?

A radiant cut engagement ring uses a rectangular or square diamond with 70 facets on the crown and pavilion. This gives the stone the large face-up area of a step-cut and the fire of a brilliant cut. The shape works in any setting style and any metal.

### What is the best setting for a radiant cut engagement ring?

The [Riviera Pavé in white gold at $1,500](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/riviera-pave-diamond-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-1-6-ct-tw-item-195326?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is the most popular and versatile option. It works with both elongated and square radiant cuts. For platinum, the [Classic Four-Prong Solitaire at $1,180](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/classic-four-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-platinum-item-194156?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) (1,815 reviews) is the most proven choice.

### How much does a radiant cut engagement ring cost?

Lab radiant rings start at [$2,012 total](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29417414?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) (1ct E-VVS1 + Classic Solitaire WG). Natural GIA radiant rings start at [$3,818 total](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/25995245?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) (1ct G-VS2 + Riviera Pavé WG). The best value in the market is the [2ct lab F-VVS1 + Riviera Pavé WG at $3,669 total](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/27801066?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational).

### What length-to-width ratio is best for a radiant cut ring?

For elongated radiant: 1.20–1.40. For square radiant: 0.95–1.05. Avoid 1.10–1.19 unless you have seen the stone in person — it can look transitional. Always confirm the ratio from the actual GIA or IGI certificate before ordering.

### Does a halo setting work on a radiant cut?

Yes. Unlike the emerald cut, a halo works on a radiant cut because the stone's corners are clipped and curved, not sharp. A round halo does not fight the radiant cut's outline the way it fights an emerald cut's hard rectangle. The [Twisted Halo in rose gold at $2,250](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/twisted-halo-diamond-engagement-ring-in-14k-rose-gold-1-3-ct-tw-item-194950?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is the strongest option.

### What clarity should I choose for a radiant cut engagement ring?

VS2 is the clarity floor for a radiant cut. The 70 brilliant-style facets scatter light and conceal inclusions that a step-cut like the emerald cut would expose. A GIA VS2 in a radiant cut is eye-clean at arm's length. You do not need VS1 unless you are buying above 2ct in natural.

### Is lab-grown radiant cut worth it for an engagement ring?

Yes, for most buyers. A [2ct IGI F-VVS1 lab radiant ring totals $3,669](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/27801066?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). The natural equivalent is $19,214. The stones are physically and optically identical. The only difference is origin. If resale value is a priority, choose natural. If not, lab is the rational choice.

### What colour grade should I buy for a radiant cut ring?

In white gold or platinum: G–H colour for natural, E–F for lab. In yellow gold or rose gold: H–I for natural, F–G for lab. Yellow and rose gold compensate for slight body warmth, so you can go one grade lower without any visible difference. The radiant cut's 70 facets also mix colour through the stone, making slight colour differences less visible than in an emerald cut.

### Should I choose elongated or square radiant for an engagement ring?

Elongated radiant (1.20–1.40 ratio) if you like ovals, emerald cuts, or finger-lengthening shapes. Square radiant (0.95–1.05 ratio) if you like cushions or princess cuts or want a bold compact look. Neither is superior. They suit different styles. Check the ratio in the certificate before ordering — do not rely on listing photos.

### How is a radiant cut different from a cushion cut?

Both are brilliant cuts with many facets. The radiant cut has clipped corners — the corner clip is what defines it legally as a radiant. The cushion cut has rounded sides and corners. The radiant tends to have more sharp, defined facet structure while cushion cuts can vary enormously in their facet pattern. Radiant cuts also tend to have a more uniform fire distribution. For a full comparison, see [Cushion Cut vs Radiant Cut Diamond](/cushion-cut-vs-radiant-cut-diamond).

### Can I see a radiant cut engagement ring before I buy?

You can request a specific stone's certificate number and HD video from most online retailers. Always review the video before buying. The HD video will confirm the actual fire and face-up appearance — this is especially important for checking the L/W ratio visually (not just numerically) and for confirming the stone is not crushed-ice dominant if you want larger flashes.

### What is The Shape Split in radiant cut rings?

The Shape Split is the decision between elongated radiant (L/W 1.20+) and square radiant (L/W under 1.10). These two stones look completely different on a finger. The elongated reads like a mini-emerald cut — long and elegant. The square reads like a cushion or princess — compact and bold. Listings often label both simply as "radiant cut" without distinguishing between them. Always read the L/W ratio from the certificate.

### What is The Total Ring Number for radiant cut engagement rings?

The Total Ring Number is your combined budget for stone plus setting, treated as one figure from the start. For a radiant cut, put 75–80% on the stone and 20–25% on the setting. The [Riviera Pavé WG at $1,500](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/riviera-pave-diamond-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-1-6-ct-tw-item-195326?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) and [Classic Four-Prong Platinum at $1,180](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/classic-four-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-platinum-item-194156?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) are the best-value settings that leave maximum budget for the stone.
